#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""hand-library-inputs — give the Library its code from root's trees and its
data from agents, as copies.

    sudo bin/hand-library-inputs               carry what is missing
    sudo bin/hand-library-inputs --dry-run     say what would happen, change nothing
    sudo bin/hand-library-inputs --check       report only; 1 if anything is still uncarried
    sudo bin/hand-library-inputs --status      the same report, changing nothing

**THE PROBLEM THIS CLOSES.** On the two- and three-account shapes the Library
runs as its own service account, with a home no other account can read
(company decision 0025 point 5). Its own job declaration, `jobs/library.toml`,
names four inputs nothing has ever put where that account can see them: the
script its `prepare` runs to mint a crew's ops credentials, the roster
source its first load reads, the seed that stocks the projects registry the
first time the Library's own database is empty, and the operator config
file every backend service reads before it will start. Before this existed,
each of those was agents' own copy or part of agents' own deploy area, which
the Library's account can no longer reach at all. `jobs/library-backup.toml`
names a fifth: `builder-backup` itself, which that job runs with
`--library-only` to back up the Library's own database, cold store and blobs,
and which — like the mint script — is not part of `agent-platform`'s own
code, so nothing else ever places it under the Library account's home either.

**WHAT IT CARRIES, AND FROM WHERE.**

1. The mint script and `builder-backup`. Both ship in this tool's own tree —
   the same root-owned copy `stand-up-backend` already runs the mint script
   from — so each is read there directly and written into the Library
   account's own `~/.local/bin`, where `jobs/library.toml`'s own `prepare`
   and `jobs/library-backup.toml`'s own `command` look for them respectively.
2. The roster source, a plain Python file read as data and never imported,
   from the root-owned `agent-platform` tree root's own record names, into
   the Library account's own deploy area, at the exact path its job
   declaration's roster-load step already names. Only where that tree
   exists: the three-account shape fetches it, and the two-account shape
   does not yet, so this carries nothing for that input there rather than
   guessing at a substitute.
3. The projects registry seed and the operator config file, each read from
   agents' own copy and written into the Library account's own state and
   config directories, create-only — a file already there, from an earlier
   run or from any other source, is left alone, byte for byte.
4. The knowledge snapshot. A child running as agents resolves
   `origin/main` to one commit, archives `projects/` out of that exact
   commit, and lists that same commit first to refuse anything a symlink
   or a submodule could smuggle in — a ref agents moves in between cannot
   change what is extracted. A child running as the Library account
   extracts that archive beside its own knowledge snapshot directory,
   refuses the whole thing if tar actually wrote anything other than a
   plain file or directory under it, and otherwise swaps it in whole by
   rename, replacing whatever snapshot was there. This refreshes on every
   run, not once: the Library's own listener later refreshes the git
   bundle and the index, never this snapshot, so this is the only thing
   that does.

**WHY THIS RUNS AS ROOT, AND WHY IT NEVER READS OR WRITES A DESTINATION BY
PATH AS ROOT.** Neither account's home is reachable from the other: the
Library's is unreadable to everyone else, and agents' is not writable by the
Library's account. Root is the only account that can reach both sides, but
reading or writing a destination directly by path as root trusts whatever
that account's own directory and file names actually are — a name root
opened could be a symlink either account planted. So every read of agents'
own files, and every read or write under the Library account's own home,
happens in a process already dropped to that account's own uid and gid,
with no supplementary group carried over, the same way
`bin/deliver-library-credentials` already does it in the other direction.
Only the root-owned trees under `/opt/builder/src` are ever read directly by
this process while still root, because those are root's own. The mint
script's and `builder-backup`'s shared shipwright tree, and the roster
source's agent-platform tree, are the ones root's record names, and every
component down to each file is checked as root's own here before anything
is read from it.

**ONLY ON THE SHAPES WHERE THE LIBRARY HAS ITS OWN ACCOUNT.** The
single-account shape runs the Library as the operator, so `place` already
puts every one of these where that account's job declaration looks; there is
nothing here for it to carry, and no other account to carry it to. An
install that has not yet provisioned the Library's own account gets the same
answer, for the same reason.

**REFUSES BEFORE READING OR WRITING ANYTHING**, naming the command that
fixes it, when the mint script's own tree is missing (`install-privileged`),
the roster source's tree exists in root's record but is missing the file
that record promised, or a destination — the Library account's own home,
agents' own home, or any single file or directory this writes under either
— is a symlink or owned by the wrong account.

**WHAT IT NEVER DOES.** It never reads the mint script, `builder-backup` or
the roster source from agents' own clones — only from a root-owned tree, or
not at all. It
never overwrites the projects seed or the operator config once something is
already there under those names; both are left alone, byte for byte. The
knowledge snapshot is the one input this refreshes every run, swapped in
whole rather than ever written into in place. It never mints anything, and
the only thing it ever deletes is the old knowledge snapshot it just
replaced.
"""

from __future__ import annotations

import argparse
import base64
import json
import os
import pwd
import re
import shutil
import stat
import subprocess
import sys
from pathlib import Path

PROG = "hand-library-inputs"

# BY ABSOLUTE PATH, the same rule `stand-up-backend` and `install-privileged`
# already hold every root-run program to: a bare name resolves through PATH,
# and an earlier PATH directory an account other than root can write would
# supply the program root runs.
GIT = "/usr/bin/git"
TAR = "/usr/bin/tar"

# Duplicated from `bin/provision-accounts`' own `LIBRARY_ACCOUNT_NAMES`
# rather than imported, the same way `bin/deliver-library-credentials`
# already duplicates it.
AGENTS = "agents"
LIBRARY_ACCOUNT_NAMES = {"macos": "_library", "linux": "library"}

# Duplicated from `bin/stand-up-backend`'s own constants of the same name:
# the root-owned prefix and root's own record of what is installed there,
# `name sha` per line.
PRIVILEGED_PREFIX = Path("/opt/builder")
INSTALLED_RECORD = PRIVILEGED_PREFIX / "src" / "installed"
ROOT_UID = 0
SHA = re.compile(r"[0-9a-f]{40}")

# Where each item lands under the Library account's own home.
MINT_DEST = Path(".local", "bin", "mint-crew-ops-credentials")
BACKUP_DEST = Path(".local", "bin", "builder-backup")
ROSTER_DEST = Path(".local", "deploy", "agent-platform", "lib", "knowledge", "knowledge.py")
SEED_DEST = Path(".local", "state", "library", "projects-registry-seed.json")
OPERATOR_DEST = Path(".config", "convivy", "operator.json")
KNOWLEDGE_SNAPSHOT_DEST = Path(".local", "state", "library", "knowledge")

# Where the roster source lives inside the root-owned agent-platform tree,
# and where agents' own copies of the data items live under its home.
ROSTER_SOURCE_REL = Path("lib", "knowledge", "knowledge.py")
AGENTS_SEED_REL = Path(".local", "state", "library", "projects-registry-seed.json")
AGENTS_OPERATOR_REL = Path(".config", "convivy", "operator.json")
AGENTS_SESSION_ENV_REL = Path(".config", "convivy", "session-agent.env")

# `git ls-tree`'s own mode strings for a symbolic link and a submodule
# (gitlink) — mirrors `install-privileged`'s own `LINK_MODES`, the check that
# already keeps either out of a root-owned tree.
LINK_MODES = {b"120000", b"160000"}
KNOWLEDGE_ARCHIVE_PATH = "projects/"
KNOWLEDGE_REF = "origin/main"

CREWS_ROOT_RE = re.compile(r"^[ \t]*CREWS_ROOT[ \t]*=[ \t]*(.*)$")


class Refused(Exception):
    """Something the operator has to decide about. Never a stack trace."""


class _Unreadable:
    """Returned by `_read_guarded` for a path that exists but could not be
    trusted as a regular file's content — a symlink, a FIFO, or anything
    else that is not a plain file. Never equal to any bytes, including
    another `_Unreadable` instance's, since the content behind it is
    unknown."""

    def __eq__(self, other):
        return False

    def __ne__(self, other):
        return True


UNREADABLE = _Unreadable()


# --- accounts, duplicated from bin/deliver-library-credentials ---------------


def library_account_name(platform: str | None = None) -> str:
    platform = platform or ("macos" if sys.platform == "darwin" else "linux")
    return LIBRARY_ACCOUNT_NAMES[platform]


def account_home(name: str) -> str | None:
    try:
        return pwd.getpwnam(name).pw_dir
    except KeyError:
        return None


def account_ids(name: str) -> tuple[int, int] | None:
    try:
        entry = pwd.getpwnam(name)
    except KeyError:
        return None
    return entry.pw_uid, entry.pw_gid


def owned_by(path: str, uid: int) -> bool:
    """Whether `path` exists, is a real directory and is owned by `uid`.

    Never follows a symlink: a symlink at an account's home would otherwise
    read or write through it to wherever it points.
    """
    try:
        info = os.lstat(path)
    except FileNotFoundError:
        return True  # nothing there yet is not foreign; it just does not exist
    if stat.S_ISLNK(info.st_mode):
        return False
    return info.st_uid == uid


# --- root's own record, duplicated from bin/stand-up-backend -----------------


def installed_sha(record_text: str | None, name: str) -> str | None:
    if record_text is None:
        return None
    for line in record_text.splitlines():
        fields = line.split()
        if len(fields) == 2 and fields[0] == name and SHA.fullmatch(fields[1]):
            return fields[1]
    return None


def _read_record(path: Path) -> str | None:
    try:
        return path.read_text(encoding="utf-8")
    except OSError:
        return None


def _owned_by_root(path: Path) -> str | None:
    try:
        info = os.lstat(path)
    except FileNotFoundError:
        return f"{path} is missing"
    if stat.S_ISLNK(info.st_mode) or info.st_uid != ROOT_UID or info.st_mode & 0o022:
        return f"{path} is not owned by root alone, or another account can write it"
    return None


def root_tree_file_problem(path: Path) -> str | None:
    """Why `path`, somewhere under a root-owned tree beneath
    `PRIVILEGED_PREFIX`, must not be trusted, or None when every component
    from it up to that prefix is.

    Lighter than `stand-up-backend`'s own `tree_problem`: this reads one file
    out of the tree and never executes anything in it, so only the path down
    to that file needs checking, not everything beside it.
    """
    top = PRIVILEGED_PREFIX
    for part in [path, *path.parents]:
        if part == top or top in part.parents:
            problem = _owned_by_root(part)
            if problem:
                return problem
    return None


# --- forking and dropping privileges, duplicated from the same tool ----------


def _drop_privileges(uid: int, gid: int) -> None:
    """Become `(uid, gid)` in THIS process, with no supplementary groups
    carried over. Called only in a child that is about to do nothing else
    but read or write into that account's own home."""
    os.setgroups([])
    os.setgid(gid)
    os.setuid(uid)


def run_as_account(uid: int, gid: int, action, *, drop=None):
    """Run `action()` — a zero-argument callable returning a JSON-able value
    — in a child that has dropped to `(uid, gid)` first, and return what it
    returns, or raise `Refused` with what it raised.

    `drop` is injected so a test that cannot become another account can stub
    it, the same way `bin/deliver-library-credentials`'s own version of this
    function already does.
    """
    if drop is None:
        drop = _drop_privileges
    read_fd, write_fd = os.pipe()
    sys.stdout.flush()
    sys.stderr.flush()
    pid = os.fork()
    if pid == 0:
        os.close(read_fd)
        try:
            drop(uid, gid)
            result = action()
            payload = json.dumps({"ok": True, "result": result}).encode("utf-8")
        except BaseException as exc:
            payload = json.dumps({"ok": False, "error": str(exc)}).encode("utf-8")
        try:
            with os.fdopen(write_fd, "wb") as out:
                out.write(len(payload).to_bytes(8, "big"))
                out.write(payload)
        finally:
            os._exit(0)
    os.close(write_fd)
    with os.fdopen(read_fd, "rb") as inp:
        header = inp.read(8)
        size = int.from_bytes(header, "big") if header else 0
        data = inp.read(size) if size else b""
    os.waitpid(pid, 0)
    decoded = json.loads(data.decode("utf-8")) if data else {"ok": False, "error": "the child reported nothing"}
    if not decoded.get("ok"):
        raise Refused(decoded.get("error") or "the child failed silently")
    return decoded.get("result")


# --- reading and writing, guarded against a symlink or a FIFO ----------------


def _read_guarded(path: Path) -> bytes | None | _Unreadable:
    """`path`'s bytes if it is a regular file, reached without following a
    symlink at its own name and without blocking on a FIFO with no writer.
    `None` for missing; `UNREADABLE` for a symlink, a FIFO, or anything else
    that is not a plain regular file — never trusted as content either way.
    """
    try:
        fd = os.open(str(path), os.O_RDONLY | os.O_NOFOLLOW | os.O_NONBLOCK)
    except FileNotFoundError:
        return None
    except OSError:
        return UNREADABLE
    try:
        if not stat.S_ISREG(os.fstat(fd).st_mode):
            os.close(fd)
            return UNREADABLE
        with os.fdopen(fd, "rb") as handle:
            return handle.read()
    except OSError:
        return UNREADABLE


def _read_root_owned(path: Path) -> bytes:
    """`path`'s bytes, trusted because it lives in a root-owned tree whose
    ownership the caller already verified. Refuses to follow a symlink at
    the file's own name regardless, as a last line of defence against a
    tree that changed underneath this process."""
    try:
        fd = os.open(str(path), os.O_RDONLY | os.O_NOFOLLOW)
    except OSError as exc:
        raise Refused(f"could not read {path}: {exc.strerror or exc}. Nothing was carried.") from exc
    with os.fdopen(fd, "rb") as handle:
        return handle.read()


def _ensure_dirs(path: Path) -> None:
    """Create every missing component of `path`, refusing at the first
    symlink or non-directory found along the way. Runs only inside a child
    already dropped to the destination account's own uid and gid, so every
    directory created here is owned by that account."""
    if path.is_symlink() or (path.exists() and not path.is_dir()):
        raise Refused(f"refusing to use {path}: it is not a plain directory. Nothing was carried.")
    if path.exists():
        return
    _ensure_dirs(path.parent)
    try:
        path.mkdir(0o700)
    except FileExistsError:
        pass


def _create_only(dest: Path, data: bytes, perm: int) -> bool:
    """Write `data` to `dest` only if nothing is there yet. Returns whether
    it wrote. A symlink or any non-regular node already at the name is
    refused, never silently left or written through; a regular file already
    there, whatever its content, is left alone byte for byte — the
    create-only rule the design states for data agents already holds a copy
    of."""
    try:
        info = os.lstat(dest)
    except FileNotFoundError:
        pass
    else:
        if stat.S_ISLNK(info.st_mode):
            raise Refused(f"refusing to use {dest}: it is a symlink, not the file itself. Nothing was carried.")
        if not stat.S_ISREG(info.st_mode):
            raise Refused(f"refusing to use {dest}: something other than a regular file is there. "
                          f"Nothing was carried.")
        return False
    # Written whole under a temporary name, then linked into place. A write
    # that fails part way (a full disk, which agents can cause, since every
    # home shares one filesystem) leaves only the temporary file, which is
    # removed, so the next run still sees the name free. Writing straight to
    # `dest` would leave a truncated file the create-only rule never retries.
    # `os.link` fails if `dest` appeared meanwhile, keeping the rule.
    tmp = dest.parent / (dest.name + ".carrying")
    try:
        os.unlink(tmp)
    except FileNotFoundError:
        pass
    fd = os.open(str(tmp), os.O_CREAT | os.O_EXCL | os.O_WRONLY | os.O_NOFOLLOW, perm)
    try:
        with os.fdopen(fd, "wb") as out:
            out.write(data)
            out.flush()
            os.fsync(out.fileno())
        os.link(tmp, dest, follow_symlinks=False)
    finally:
        try:
            os.unlink(tmp)
        except FileNotFoundError:
            pass
    return True


def _write_if_different(dest: Path, data: bytes, perm: int) -> bool:
    """Write `data` to `dest`, atomically, only if it is not already there.
    A symlink or any non-regular node already at the name is refused, never
    written through."""
    try:
        info = os.lstat(dest)
    except FileNotFoundError:
        info = None
    if info is not None:
        if stat.S_ISLNK(info.st_mode):
            raise Refused(f"refusing to use {dest}: it is a symlink, not the file itself. Nothing was carried.")
        if not stat.S_ISREG(info.st_mode):
            raise Refused(f"refusing to use {dest}: something other than a regular file is there. "
                          f"Nothing was carried.")
    existing = _read_guarded(dest)
    if existing == data:
        return False
    tmp = dest.parent / (dest.name + ".carrying")
    try:
        os.unlink(tmp)
    except FileNotFoundError:
        pass
    fd = os.open(str(tmp), os.O_CREAT | os.O_EXCL | os.O_WRONLY | os.O_NOFOLLOW, perm)
    with os.fdopen(fd, "wb") as out:
        out.write(data)
    os.replace(tmp, dest)
    return True


# --- the code items: the mint script, and the roster source on shape three ---


def default_mint_script(record_text: str | None) -> Path:
    """`payload/bin/mint-crew-ops-credentials` in the root-owned shipwright
    tree root's record names. Never resolved from this file's own location:
    a copy run from a checkout another account can edit would otherwise
    hand the Library that account's code."""
    sha = installed_sha(record_text, "shipwright")
    if sha is None:
        raise Refused(f"{INSTALLED_RECORD} names no shipwright commit, so there is no root-owned "
                      f"mint script to carry. Re-run install-privileged. Nothing was carried.")
    return PRIVILEGED_PREFIX / "src" / f"shipwright@{sha}" / "payload" / "bin" / "mint-crew-ops-credentials"


def default_backup_script(record_text: str | None) -> Path:
    """`payload/bin/builder-backup` in the same root-owned shipwright tree
    `default_mint_script` reads from — `jobs/library-backup.toml`'s own copy,
    never `{deploy}/builder-payload`'s, which the Library account cannot
    reach at all."""
    sha = installed_sha(record_text, "shipwright")
    if sha is None:
        raise Refused(f"{INSTALLED_RECORD} names no shipwright commit, so there is no root-owned "
                      f"builder-backup to carry. Re-run install-privileged. Nothing was carried.")
    return PRIVILEGED_PREFIX / "src" / f"shipwright@{sha}" / "payload" / "bin" / "builder-backup"


def load_mint_script(script: Path | None = None, record_text: str | None = None) -> bytes:
    """The mint script's bytes. With no `script`, it is the copy in root's
    shipwright tree, and every component down to it must be root's own."""
    if script is None:
        script = default_mint_script(record_text)
        problem = root_tree_file_problem(script)
        if problem:
            raise Refused(f"{problem}. Re-run install-privileged. Nothing was carried.")
    if not script.is_file():
        raise Refused(f"{script} does not exist; this release's own copy is missing. Nothing was carried.")
    return _read_root_owned(script)


def load_backup_script(script: Path | None = None, record_text: str | None = None) -> bytes:
    """`builder-backup`'s bytes, the same way `load_mint_script` reads the
    mint script: from root's shipwright tree alone, with no `script` given."""
    if script is None:
        script = default_backup_script(record_text)
        problem = root_tree_file_problem(script)
        if problem:
            raise Refused(f"{problem}. Re-run install-privileged. Nothing was carried.")
    if not script.is_file():
        raise Refused(f"{script} does not exist; this release's own copy is missing. Nothing was carried.")
    return _read_root_owned(script)


def agent_platform_tree(record_text: str | None) -> Path | None:
    """The root-owned `agent-platform` tree root's record names, or None
    when the record names none — the ordinary case on the two-account
    shape, which does not fetch that repository yet."""
    sha = installed_sha(record_text, "agent-platform")
    if sha is None:
        return None
    return PRIVILEGED_PREFIX / "src" / f"agent-platform@{sha}"


def load_roster_source(record_text: str | None) -> bytes | None:
    """The roster source's bytes, or None when the tree that would hold it
    is not fetched on this shape at all. A tree that IS recorded but does
    not hold the file, or is not root's own, is a refusal — that is a
    broken or tampered install, never an ordinary absence."""
    tree = agent_platform_tree(record_text)
    if tree is None:
        return None
    source = tree / ROSTER_SOURCE_REL
    problem = root_tree_file_problem(source)
    if problem:
        raise Refused(f"{problem}. Re-run install-privileged. Nothing was carried.")
    if not source.is_file():
        raise Refused(f"{source} is missing, so there is no roster source to carry. "
                      f"Re-run install-privileged. Nothing was carried.")
    return _read_root_owned(source)


# --- the data items: the projects seed and the operator config file ----------


def _read_agents_side(agents_home: Path) -> dict:
    """Everything this reads FROM agents — called only inside a child
    already dropped to agents' own uid and gid. Each file's bytes cross back
    to root as base64, inside the JSON `run_as_account` already carries;
    `None` for a missing, symlinked, or otherwise untrusted source — a
    planted link on agents' side never supplies fake content, it simply
    leaves the Library's own side with nothing to carry for that item."""
    seed = _read_guarded(agents_home / AGENTS_SEED_REL)
    operator = _read_guarded(agents_home / AGENTS_OPERATOR_REL)
    return {
        "projects_seed": base64.b64encode(seed).decode("ascii") if isinstance(seed, bytes) else None,
        "operator_config": base64.b64encode(operator).decode("ascii") if isinstance(operator, bytes) else None,
    }


def _b64_decode(value: str | None) -> bytes | None:
    return base64.b64decode(value) if value is not None else None


def library_items(mint_bytes: bytes, backup_bytes: bytes, roster_bytes: bytes | None,
                  seed_bytes: bytes | None, operator_bytes: bytes | None) -> list[tuple]:
    """`(name, dest, data, kind, perm)` for every item this hands to the
    Library account. `kind` is `"diff"` (write when the destination
    differs — code, which a later release may replace) or `"create"` (write
    only when the destination is absent — data agents already holds a copy
    of, per the design's create-only rule)."""
    items = [
        ("mint-crew-ops-credentials", MINT_DEST, mint_bytes, "diff", 0o700),
        ("builder-backup", BACKUP_DEST, backup_bytes, "diff", 0o700),
    ]
    if roster_bytes is not None:
        items.append(("knowledge.py", ROSTER_DEST, roster_bytes, "diff", 0o644))
    if seed_bytes is not None:
        items.append(("projects-registry-seed.json", SEED_DEST, seed_bytes, "create", 0o600))
    if operator_bytes is not None:
        items.append(("operator.json", OPERATOR_DEST, operator_bytes, "create", 0o600))
    return items


def plan_in_library(library_home: Path, items: list[tuple]) -> list[str]:
    """Which of `items` the Library account does not yet hold as given.
    Called only inside a child already dropped to the Library account's own
    uid and gid. Writes nothing."""
    pending = []
    for name, dest, data, kind, _perm in items:
        existing = _read_guarded(library_home / dest)
        if kind == "create":
            if existing is None or existing is UNREADABLE:
                pending.append(name)
        elif existing != data:
            pending.append(name)
    return pending


def do_in_library(library_home: Path, items: list[tuple]) -> list[str]:
    """Write every pending item in `items`, and return the names actually
    written. Called only inside a child already dropped to the Library
    account's own uid and gid."""
    written = []
    for name, dest, data, kind, perm in items:
        full = library_home / dest
        _ensure_dirs(full.parent)
        wrote = _create_only(full, data, perm) if kind == "create" else _write_if_different(full, data, perm)
        if wrote:
            written.append(name)
    return written


# --- the knowledge snapshot ---------------------------------------------------


def _crews_root(agents_home: Path) -> str | None:
    """The Builder root agents' own `root()` resolves to — read the same
    way it does: the first `CREWS_ROOT=` line of agents' own
    `session-agent.env`, not through the linked `builder-root` command,
    which is not placed yet when this step runs (`link` runs after it)."""
    content = _read_guarded(agents_home / AGENTS_SESSION_ENV_REL)
    if not isinstance(content, bytes):
        return None
    for line in content.decode("utf-8", "replace").splitlines():
        match = CREWS_ROOT_RE.match(line)
        if match:
            value = match.group(1).rstrip(" \t")
            return value or None
    return None


def knowledge_repo_path(agents_home: Path) -> str | None:
    """The knowledge repository agents already holds, or None when agents
    has no recorded Builder root yet, or no repository under it — both
    ordinary on a machine where this step runs before that repository
    exists."""
    root = _crews_root(agents_home)
    if root is None or not os.path.isabs(root):
        return None
    repo = Path(root) / "knowledge"
    if not (repo / ".git").is_dir():
        return None
    return str(repo)


def refused_knowledge_entries(listing: bytes) -> str | None:
    """Why the knowledge archive must be refused whole, or None when every
    entry under `projects/` is a plain file or directory at a path that
    stays under it. Mirrors `install-privileged`'s own `extract()`: a
    symlink or a submodule (gitlink) entry is refused outright, and so is a
    path carrying a `..` component, which a crafted tree object could still
    hold even though an ordinary commit never produces one."""
    for entry in listing.split(b"\0"):
        if not entry:
            continue
        meta, _, path = entry.partition(b"\t")
        mode = meta.split(b" ")[0]
        text = path.decode("utf-8", "replace")
        if mode in LINK_MODES:
            kind = "a symbolic link" if mode == b"120000" else "a submodule (gitlink)"
            return f"the knowledge archive holds {text!r} as {kind}"
        if text.startswith("/") or any(part == ".." for part in Path(text).parts):
            return f"the knowledge archive holds {text!r}, which escapes its own directory"
    return None


def resolve_knowledge_commit(repo: str) -> str:
    """The commit `origin/main` names in `repo` at this instant, resolved
    once so the same commit is both checked and archived — a ref agents
    moves between those two steps can no longer change what is extracted.
    Refuses anything git reports that is not exactly 40 lowercase hex
    characters. Called only inside a child already dropped to agents' own
    uid and gid."""
    done = subprocess.run(
        [GIT, "-C", repo, "rev-parse", "--verify", f"{KNOWLEDGE_REF}^{{commit}}"],
        capture_output=True, check=False,
    )
    if done.returncode != 0:
        raise Refused(f"git could not resolve {KNOWLEDGE_REF} in the knowledge repository: "
                      f"{done.stderr.decode('utf-8', 'replace').strip()}. Nothing was carried.")
    commit = done.stdout.decode("ascii", "replace").strip()
    if not SHA.fullmatch(commit):
        raise Refused(f"git reported {commit!r} for {KNOWLEDGE_REF}, not a 40-character lowercase hex "
                      f"commit. Nothing was carried.")
    return commit


def refused_knowledge_entries_for(repo: str, commit: str) -> str | None:
    """`refused_knowledge_entries`, fed by listing `commit` under
    `projects/` — the same commit `resolve_knowledge_commit` already
    resolved `origin/main` to, never the ref again, so a ref agents moves
    after that point cannot change what this lists. Called only inside a
    child already dropped to agents' own uid and gid."""
    done = subprocess.run(
        [GIT, "-C", repo, "ls-tree", "-r", "-z", "--full-tree", commit, "--", KNOWLEDGE_ARCHIVE_PATH],
        capture_output=True, check=False,
    )
    if done.returncode != 0:
        return (f"git could not list {KNOWLEDGE_ARCHIVE_PATH} at {commit} in the knowledge repository: "
                f"{done.stderr.decode('utf-8', 'replace').strip()}")
    return refused_knowledge_entries(done.stdout)


def refused_extracted_entries(staged: Path) -> str | None:
    """Why the tree tar just extracted under `staged` must be refused
    whole, or None when every entry inside it is a plain file or directory
    at a path that stays under it. Checks what tar actually wrote rather
    than only what `refused_knowledge_entries_for` listed beforehand — the
    check that holds whatever tar was fed, however that differs from the
    stream the listing looked at. Called only inside a child already
    dropped to the Library account's own uid and gid."""
    root = staged.resolve()
    for dirpath, dirnames, filenames in os.walk(staged, followlinks=False):
        for name in dirnames + filenames:
            path = Path(dirpath) / name
            info = os.lstat(path)
            if not (stat.S_ISDIR(info.st_mode) or stat.S_ISREG(info.st_mode)):
                return f"the extracted knowledge snapshot holds {path}, which is not a plain file or directory"
            real = path.resolve()
            if real != root and root not in real.parents:
                return f"the extracted knowledge snapshot holds {path}, which escapes its own directory"
    return None


def _swap_in_knowledge_snapshot(staged: Path, dest: Path) -> None:
    """Put `staged` at `dest`, whole. When nothing is there yet, a plain
    rename does it. When a previous snapshot already is — the ordinary
    case on a rerun — rename it aside first, rename `staged` into `dest`,
    then remove the one set aside; if that second rename fails, rename the
    old one back so `dest` is never left missing. Runs only inside a child
    already dropped to the Library account's own uid and gid, after
    `refused_extracted_entries` has already passed."""
    if not dest.exists():
        os.rename(staged, dest)
        return
    old = dest.parent / f".{dest.name}.old-{os.getpid()}"
    os.rename(dest, old)
    try:
        os.rename(staged, dest)
    except OSError:
        os.rename(old, dest)
        raise
    shutil.rmtree(old, ignore_errors=True)


def _knowledge_state(dest: Path) -> str:
    """`"absent"`, `"present"` (a plain directory already there — due for
    a refresh, not left alone), or `"occupied"` (something else is there —
    refused). Called only inside a child already dropped to the Library
    account's own uid and gid."""
    try:
        info = os.lstat(dest)
    except FileNotFoundError:
        return "absent"
    if stat.S_ISDIR(info.st_mode) and not stat.S_ISLNK(info.st_mode):
        return "present"
    return "occupied"


def _run_archive_pipeline(agents_uid: int, agents_gid: int, repo: str, commit: str,
                          library_uid: int, library_gid: int, dest: Path, drop, verb: str) -> str:
    """Fork a child as agents that archives `commit` under `projects/` to a
    pipe — the same commit `refused_knowledge_entries_for` already
    checked, never `origin/main` again, so a ref agents moves in between
    cannot change what is extracted — and a child as the Library account
    that extracts that pipe beside `dest`, refuses the whole thing unless
    every entry tar actually wrote is a plain file or directory that stays
    under it, and otherwise swaps it in whole by rename. Root only forks
    the two children and waits on them — it never opens either end of the
    pipe itself, and never reads or writes `dest` directly."""
    read_fd, write_fd = os.pipe()
    sys.stdout.flush()
    sys.stderr.flush()

    archive_pid = os.fork()
    if archive_pid == 0:
        os.close(read_fd)
        try:
            drop(agents_uid, agents_gid)
            os.dup2(write_fd, 1)
        except BaseException:
            os._exit(1)
        os.close(write_fd)
        try:
            os.execv(GIT, [GIT, "-C", repo, "archive", "--format=tar", commit, "--", KNOWLEDGE_ARCHIVE_PATH])
        except OSError:
            pass
        os._exit(1)
    os.close(write_fd)

    staged = dest.parent / f".{dest.name}.new-{archive_pid}"
    sys.stdout.flush()
    sys.stderr.flush()
    extract_pid = os.fork()
    if extract_pid == 0:
        try:
            drop(library_uid, library_gid)
            _ensure_dirs(dest.parent)
            staged.mkdir(mode=0o700)
            os.dup2(read_fd, 0)
            os.close(read_fd)
            done = subprocess.run([TAR, "-x", "-f", "-", "-C", str(staged)], cwd="/", check=False)
            if done.returncode != 0:
                raise RuntimeError(f"tar exited {done.returncode} while extracting the knowledge archive")
            problem = refused_extracted_entries(staged)
            if problem:
                raise RuntimeError(problem)
            _swap_in_knowledge_snapshot(staged, dest)
        except BaseException as exc:
            print(f"{PROG}: could not seed the knowledge snapshot: {exc}", file=sys.stderr)
            shutil.rmtree(staged, ignore_errors=True)
            os._exit(1)
        os._exit(0)
    os.close(read_fd)

    _, archive_status = os.waitpid(archive_pid, 0)
    _, extract_status = os.waitpid(extract_pid, 0)
    if extract_status != 0 or archive_status != 0:
        raise Refused(f"could not seed the Library's own knowledge snapshot from {repo}; "
                      f"see the error above. Nothing was carried.")
    return f"{verb} {dest} from {repo}@{commit}"


def carry_knowledge_snapshot(agents_uid: int, agents_gid: int, agents_home: Path,
                             library_uid: int, library_gid: int, library_home: Path,
                             *, dry_run: bool, drop=None) -> str:
    """Refresh the Library's own knowledge snapshot from agents' own
    knowledge repository — a one-line report of what happened or would
    happen. Runs every time the operator reruns this step, replacing
    whatever plain directory is already there whole, by rename, never
    leaving a partial tree visible: the profile load that reads this
    directory deletes a project's rows when its directory is missing, so a
    half-written one must never be seen.
    """
    drop = drop or _drop_privileges
    dest = library_home / KNOWLEDGE_SNAPSHOT_DEST
    state = run_as_account(library_uid, library_gid, lambda: _knowledge_state(dest), drop=drop)
    if state == "occupied":
        raise Refused(f"refusing to use {dest}: something other than a plain directory is there. "
                      f"Nothing was carried.")
    repo = run_as_account(agents_uid, agents_gid, lambda: knowledge_repo_path(agents_home), drop=drop)
    if repo is None:
        return "agents has no knowledge repository yet (or no recorded Builder root); nothing to seed"
    if dry_run:
        verb = "would refresh" if state == "present" else "would seed"
        return f"{verb} {dest} from {repo}"
    commit = run_as_account(agents_uid, agents_gid, lambda: resolve_knowledge_commit(repo), drop=drop)
    problem = run_as_account(agents_uid, agents_gid, lambda: refused_knowledge_entries_for(repo, commit), drop=drop)
    if problem:
        raise Refused(f"{problem}. Nothing was carried.")
    verb = "refreshed" if state == "present" else "seeded"
    return _run_archive_pipeline(agents_uid, agents_gid, repo, commit, library_uid, library_gid, dest, drop, verb)


def knowledge_pending(agents_uid: int, agents_gid: int, agents_home: Path,
                      library_uid: int, library_gid: int, library_home: Path, drop=None) -> bool:
    drop = drop or _drop_privileges
    dest = library_home / KNOWLEDGE_SNAPSHOT_DEST
    state = run_as_account(library_uid, library_gid, lambda: _knowledge_state(dest), drop=drop)
    if state != "absent":
        return False
    repo = run_as_account(agents_uid, agents_gid, lambda: knowledge_repo_path(agents_home), drop=drop)
    return repo is not None


def main(argv: list[str]) -> int:
    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(
        prog=PROG,
        description="Give the Library its own code from root's trees and its own data from agents, as copies.",
    )
    mode = parser.add_mutually_exclusive_group()
    mode.add_argument("--dry-run", action="store_true", help="say what would happen, change nothing")
    mode.add_argument("--check", action="store_true", help="report only; 1 if anything is still uncarried")
    mode.add_argument("--status", action="store_true", help="the same report, changing nothing")
    args = parser.parse_args(argv)

    if os.geteuid() != 0:
        print(f"{PROG}: refusing — this needs root, to read root's own trees and reach both "
              f"the Library's account and agents'. Nothing was carried.", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2

    library_name = library_account_name()
    library_home_str = account_home(library_name)
    if library_home_str is None:
        print(f"{PROG}: no {library_name} account on this machine — nothing to carry. Either "
              f"this is the single-account shape, where the Library runs as the operator, or "
              f"the Library's own account has not been provisioned yet.")
        return 0

    agents_home_str = account_home(AGENTS)
    if agents_home_str is None:
        print(f"{PROG}: refusing — {library_name} exists but {AGENTS} does not. Run "
              f"provision-accounts with this shape first. Nothing was carried.", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2

    library_ids = account_ids(library_name)
    agents_ids = account_ids(AGENTS)
    assert library_ids is not None and agents_ids is not None  # just resolved by name above

    if not owned_by(library_home_str, library_ids[0]):
        owner = os.lstat(library_home_str).st_uid
        print(f"{PROG}: refusing — {library_home_str} (home of {library_name}) is owned by uid "
              f"{owner}, not its own account. Something else made it; this will not read from "
              f"it or write into it. Nothing was carried.", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    if not owned_by(agents_home_str, agents_ids[0]):
        owner = os.lstat(agents_home_str).st_uid
        print(f"{PROG}: refusing — {agents_home_str} (home of {AGENTS}) is owned by uid "
              f"{owner}, not its own account. Something else made it; this will not read from "
              f"it. Nothing was carried.", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2

    library_home = Path(library_home_str)
    agents_home = Path(agents_home_str)
    library_uid, library_gid = library_ids
    agents_uid, agents_gid = agents_ids

    try:
        record_text = _read_record(INSTALLED_RECORD)
        mint_bytes = load_mint_script(record_text=record_text)
        backup_bytes = load_backup_script(record_text=record_text)
        roster_bytes = load_roster_source(record_text)
        agents_data = run_as_account(agents_uid, agents_gid, lambda: _read_agents_side(agents_home))
    except Refused as exc:
        print(f"{PROG}: refusing — {exc}", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2

    seed_bytes = _b64_decode(agents_data.get("projects_seed"))
    operator_bytes = _b64_decode(agents_data.get("operator_config"))
    items = library_items(mint_bytes, backup_bytes, roster_bytes, seed_bytes, operator_bytes)

    try:
        if args.check or args.status:
            pending = run_as_account(library_uid, library_gid, lambda: plan_in_library(library_home, items))
            snap_pending = knowledge_pending(agents_uid, agents_gid, agents_home,
                                             library_uid, library_gid, library_home)
            if pending:
                print(f"{PROG}: {len(pending)} input(s) not yet carried: {', '.join(pending)}")
            else:
                print(f"{PROG}: every code and data input this hands the Library is carried")
            # A present snapshot is carried, so `--check` passes on it, but it is
            # not final: every run replaces it whole from the current commit.
            print(f"{PROG}: the knowledge snapshot is "
                  f"{'not yet seeded' if snap_pending else 'present; every run refreshes it whole'}")
            return 1 if (args.check and (pending or snap_pending)) else 0

        if args.dry_run:
            pending = run_as_account(library_uid, library_gid, lambda: plan_in_library(library_home, items))
            for name, _dest, _data, _kind, _perm in items:
                verb = "would carry" if name in pending else "already carries"
                print(f"{PROG}: {verb} {name}")
            snapshot_report = carry_knowledge_snapshot(
                agents_uid, agents_gid, agents_home, library_uid, library_gid, library_home, dry_run=True)
            print(f"{PROG}: {snapshot_report}")
            return 0

        written = run_as_account(library_uid, library_gid, lambda: do_in_library(library_home, items))
        if written:
            for name in written:
                print(f"{PROG}: carried {name}")
        else:
            print(f"{PROG}: nothing to carry — the Library already has every code and data "
                  f"input this hands it")
        snapshot_report = carry_knowledge_snapshot(
            agents_uid, agents_gid, agents_home, library_uid, library_gid, library_home, dry_run=False)
        print(f"{PROG}: {snapshot_report}")
    except Refused as exc:
        print(f"{PROG}: refusing — {exc}", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    return 0


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main(sys.argv[1:]))
